{"id":"f1a5979c-933d-4235-878f-e875d5c23866","object":"chat.completion","created":1784886376,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    required_symbols = set(case['required_symbols'])\\n    node_by_id = {n['id']: n for n in nodes}\\n    children = {}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        pid = n.get('parent')\\n        if pid is not None:\\n            children.setdefault(pid, []).append(n['id'])\\n    symbol_ids = {}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        sym = n['symbol']\\n        symbol_ids.setdefault(sym, []).append(n['id'])\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n['depth'], n['id']))\\n    removed_ids = set()\\n    removal_order = []\\n    for n in sorted_nodes:\\n        nid = n['id']\\n        if not n.get('removable', False):\\n            continue\\n        if n.get('parent') is None:\\n            continue\\n        if n['symbol'] in required_symbols:\\n            continue\\n        child_ids = children.get(nid, [])\\n        if any(c not in removed_ids for c in child_ids):\\n            continue\\n        ok = True\\n        for sym in required_symbols:\\n            ids_for_sym = symbol_ids.get(sym, [])\\n            if not any((i != nid and i not in removed_ids) for i in ids_for_sym):\\n                ok = False\\n                break\\n        if not ok:\\n            continue\\n        removed_ids.add(nid)\\n        removal_order.append(nid)\\n    retained_ids = sorted([nid for nid in node_by_id if nid not in removed_ids])\\n    return {'removed_node_ids': removal_order, 'retained_node_ids': retained_ids}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to write Python code for solve(case) that implements grammar_guided_node_reduction. The task is SE-PE-01, based on the described mechanism: reduce a parse tree (nodes with parent, depth, symbol, removable flag, utility) while preserving required symbols. The algorithm: depth-first, consid