al order). Retained_node_ids sorted.\n\nGiven the test fixtures, all have same structure. We need to produce removed_node_ids that are the nodes that are removed according to the algorithm. Let's analyze one case:\n\nCase fg1-se-pe-01-b-000:\nNodes:\nroot (depth0, removable false)\nn1 (depth1, parent root, symbol s1, removable false)\nn2 (depth1, parent root, symbol s2, removable true)\nn3 (depth1, parent root, symbol s0, removable false)\nn4 (depth2, parent n2, symbol s1, removable true)\nn5 (depth2, parent n3, symbol s2, removable false)\nn6 (depth2, parent n1, symbol s0, removable true)\n\nRequired symbols: root, s1\n\nWe need to consider deeper nodes first: depths: 2 then 1 then 0. Depth2 nodes: n4, n5, n6. Order by node ID tie break? n4, n5, n6 (alphabetically). For each removable node: n4 removable, n5 not, n6 removable.\nCheck n4: symbol s1. If we remove n4, will required symbols still be present? Required symbols: root (present at root), s1. n4 is s1, but there is also n1 which is s1. So s1 is still present (n1). So tentatively remove n4? But rule: \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\" n4 has no children? It is leaf? Depth2 and no children listed. So it's leaf. So removing n4 is allowed. Also \"Never remove a node with retained children\" – no children. So we can remove n4. So n4 is removed.\nNext n5 not removable, skip.\nNext n6 removable, symbol s0. s0 is not required. Required symbols: root, s1. root remains, s1 remains (n1). So removing n6 allowed. No children. So we tentatively remove n6.\nNow depth1: n1 (not removable), n2 (removable), n3 (not removable). n2: symbol s2, not required. Before removing n2, check if all required symbols still represented after removal. n2 has a child n4 which was already removed. But if we remove n2, its children? n4 is removed, but n2 might have other children? It only had n4. If we remove n2, the entire subtree of n2 is removed. n2's subtree contained n4 (already removed). So rem