    # map symbol to list of ids\n    symbol_ids = {}\n    for n in nodes:\n        sym = n['symbol']\n        symbol_ids.setdefault(sym, []).append(n['id'])\n    \n    # sort nodes by depth descending, then id ascending\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n['depth'], n['id']))\n    \n    removed_ids = set()\n    removal_order = []\n    \n    for n in sorted_nodes:\n        nid = n['id']\n        if not n.get('removable', False):\n            continue\n        if n.get('parent') is None:  # root\n            continue\n        if n['symbol'] in required_symbols:\n            continue\n        # check retained children\n        child_ids = children.get(nid, [])\n        if any(c not in removed_ids for c in child_ids):\n            continue\n        # check required symbols still present\n        ok = True\n        for sym in required_symbols:\n            ids_for_sym = symbol_ids.get(sym, [])\n            # find if any id for this symbol is not removed and not nid\n            if not any((i != nid and i not in removed_ids) for i in ids_for_sym):\n                ok = False\n                break\n        if not ok:\n            continue\n        # remove\n        removed_ids.add(nid)\n        removal_order.append(nid)\n    \n    retained_ids = sorted([nid for nid in node_by_id if nid not in removed_ids])\n    return {\n        'removed_node_ids': removal_order,\n        'retained_node_ids': retained_ids\n    }\n\nNote: The output requires retained_node_ids to be sorted. We'll sort.\n\nNow we need to output {\"implementation\": \"...\"} with escaped string.\n\nWe'll produce the final JSON.\n\nBut we must ensure no extra text, just JSON object.\n\nLet's construct the Python source string. Escape newlines as \\n, backslashes as \\\\, quotes as \\\".\n\nWe'll write it as a single line or multiline? Easier to use multiline string in Python and then escape when converting to JSON. But we need to manually escape. Best to write the code in a string in Python and then use json.dumps to escape. But we are generating the response manually, so we need to escape properly.\n\nI'll write the code in a raw string and then embed it.\n\nActually, I can generate the JSON by first building the implementation string in a Python script and printing the JSON. But since I am the AI, I'll construct it manually.\n\nGiven the complexity, I'll produce the escaped string carefully.\n\nLet me write the code as a single string with explicit \\n.\n\nI'll write it as:\n\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case['nodes']\n    required_symbols = set(case['required_symbols'])\n    node_by_id = {n['id']: n for n in nodes}\n    children = {}\n    for n in nodes:\n        pid = n.get('parent')\n        if pid is not None:\n            children.setdefault(pid, []).append(n['id'])\n    symbol_ids = {}\n    for n in nodes:\n        sym = n['symbol']\n        symbol_ids.setdefault(sym, []).append(n['id'])\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n['depth'], n['id']))\n    removed_ids = set()\n    removal_order = []\n    for n in sorted_nodes:\n        nid = n['id']\n        if not n.get('removable', False):\n            continue\n        if n.get('parent') is None:\n            continue\n        if n['symbol'] in required_symbols:\n            continue\n        child_ids = children.get(nid, [])\n        if any(c not in removed_ids for c in child_ids):\n            continue\n        ok = True\n        for sym in required_symbols:\n            ids_for_sym = symbol_ids.get(sym, [])\n            if not any((i != nid and i not in removed_ids) for i in ids_for_sym):\n                ok = False\n                break\n        if not ok:\n            continue\n        removed_ids.add(nid)\n        removal_order.append(nid)\n    retained_ids = sorted([nid for nid in node_by_id if nid not in removed_ids])\n    return {'removed_node_ids': removal_order, 'retained_node_ids': retained_ids}\n\nNow we need to escape it for JSON. Replace backslashes with double backslash